the program. The department also seeks candidates who will contribute to the University’s general education curriculum with its emphasis on a common First Year Seminar and core curriculum courses that enhance students’ critical thinking, and the College’s support of interdisciplinary program of study. Candidates interviewing on campus must have unofficial transcript (UG & G) forwarded to the Director of the School of Nursing by their degree-granting institutions prior to the interview on campus. Location MU - Marshall University Salary Range Salary is commensurate upon education, experience and internal equity Qualifications Must be able to perform all essential job duties as outlined in the job description. Required Qualifications Education Applicants must have a master’s degree in nursing. Must hold an unencumbered license (or be eligible for licensure) as an RN in West Virginia. Experience A minimum of three (3) years of recent experience in pediatric nursing is required. A minimum of two (2) years of teaching experience is preferred. Preferred Qualifications Education Doctoral degree in nursing is preferred. Experience Posting Detail Information Posting Number MU1786F Open Date 03/26/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master's Degree in Nursing? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Unofficial Transcripts CV or Resume Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
