      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant Office of Career Education",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant Office of Career Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Graduate Assistant Office of Career Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Graduate Assistant Office of Career Education Description of GA Assignment GA: Clinical Practice - The department will assign you to various tasks that will require you to provide professional service to MU students, clients of a MU Clinic, or other individuals in need of professional services provided by the office. Job Description Summary Looking for a full-time grad student beginning Fall 2026 who is interested in working with students and employers in a career-focused setting. This position will be working in an office environment and duties may include: * Greet students and other guests as they enter the door and practice social distancing * Respond to students/alumni & employer questions and concerns * Triage students and calls to appropriate staff * Schedule appointments * Assist in the promotion and marketing of career-related events, including the use of Career Education social media accounts, information tables, hanging flyers, etc. * Career-related presentations to student groups and organization You will be trained to review resumes, cover letters, and other documents as well as assist students and employers in the lobby with registrations, uploading documents, and sending out employment information. You will receive a $10 hourly wage as well as a 70% tuition stipend (no fees). Department Office of Career Education - MU3102 Location MU - Marshall University Semester Fall Semester Hours Per Week Full Time (20 hrs a week) Qualifications Required Qualifications Education Bachelor’s degree, pursuing a Master’s Degree Experience Previous work experience 