    "https://marshall.peopleadmin.com/postings/29970": {
      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Medicine, Cardiac Imaging Noninvasive Cardiologist ( 3 positions available )",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Medicine, Cardiac Imaging Noninvasive Cardiologist ( 3 positions available ) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Assistant Professor of Medicine, Cardiac Imaging Noninvasive Cardiologist ( 3 positions available ) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Get to Know Us! Marshall University is a public comprehensive university with a rich history as one of the oldest institutions of higher learning in West Virginia. Founded in 1837 and named after Chief Justice John Marshall, definer of the Constitution, Marshall University advances the public good through innovative, accredited educational programs. We are located in downtown Huntington, West Virginia, with additional locations in South Charleston, Point Pleasant, Teays Valley and Beckley. Marshall University’s mission, inspired by our Vision and Creed, includes a commitment to: Offer a wide range of high quality, affordable, and accessible undergraduate, graduate, and professional education that prepares students to think, learn, work, and live in an evolving global society. Create opportunities and experiences to foster understanding and appreciation of the rich diversity of thought and culture. Maintain a dynamic intellectual, artistic, and cultural life by promoting and supporting research and creative activities by undergraduates, graduates, and faculty. Contribute to the quality of life of the community, region, and beyond through applied research, economic development, health care, and cultural enrichment. Cultivate the development of an inclusive, just, and equitable community. Come Meet Marshall and discover what it means to be part of the Marshall University family! Come join our Herd! We are committed to attracting and retaining quality faculty and staff. In doing so, Marshall University offers outstanding benefit packages to eligible employees only. (E-Class in the job posting). Marshall University Research Corporation ( MURC ) employees have different benefit options than those listed below. Work week is 37.5 hrs. A great highlight in December is that Marshall University employees receive almost two weeks off for Winter Break! Holidays – Employees receive 13 Paid Holidays Annual and Sick Leave – Classified Staff, Non-Classified Staff and 12-month Faculty earn up to 24 days of annual leave per year (max 360 hours) and up to 18 days of sick leave per year. ) Employee Leave Health Insurance – Marshall University offers health insurance through West Virginia Public Employees Insurance Agency ( PEIA ). There are seven (7) health benefit plans. Educational/Tuition Benefits – Marshall University provides tuition benefits to regular employees (after probationary period) and their dependent children. Retirement Plans – Marshall University offers retirement through Teachers Insurance and Annuity Association ( TIAA ). Full-time benefits eligible employees must participate in the mandated retirement plan (401(a)). Life Insurance – Basic term life insurance ($10,000) at no cost and may purchase optional life insurance coverage with pre-tax earnings. Wellness Programs – PEIA provides various care management programs and the Pathways to Wellness program. We are . . . Marshall! Position Information Banner Position Number 002498 Position Title Assistant Professor of Medicine, Cardiac Imaging Noninvasive Cardiologist ( 3 positions available ) Classification Title Assistant Professor Department SOM-Cardiovascular Services - MU9452 Job Description Marshall University Joan C. Edwards School of Medicine’s Department of Cardiovascular Services is seeking a qualified cardiologist specializing in advanced cardiac imaging to join its faculty. This position will be responsible for development of the Cardiac MRI program at the institution. Marshall Cardiology is a close-knit, dependable community of physicians looking for our newest partners. We are a busy growing practice, also looking to hire more interventionalists, Electrophysiologists and noninvasive cardiologists. • Provider at one primary site, establishing an MRI program at the institution • Providers rotate at 2 hospitals and 1 clinic site in the Huntington, WV area • Call is 1:6, weekends only, shared between all attendings with fellows participating in rounds. • Teaching formally and informally for the 12 cardiology fellows. • Multiple collaborative research opportunities with translational, biomedical sciences programs. This position will combine clinical care with formal and in-formal teaching activities for cardiology fellows, residents and medical students and an appointment to the Marshall University Joan C. Edwards School of Medicine (with ACGME -approved general cardiology and interventional fellowship programs). This appointment is available for Assistant or Associate Professor, nontenured clinical track or tenure-track educator for qualified applicants. Location MUSOM - Marshall University School of Medicine Salary Range Commensurate with education and experience Qualifications Must be able to perform all essential job duties as outlined in the job description. Required Qualifications Education Experience Preferred Qualifications Education Experience Posting Detail Information Posting Number MU0949F Open Date 03/03/2021 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
