      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant - 1 positions available",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant - 1 positions available Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Graduate Assistant - 1 positions available Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Graduate Assistant - 1 positions available Description of GA Assignment GA: Clinical Practice - The department will assign you to various tasks that will require you to provide professional service to MU students, clients of a MU Clinic, or other individuals in need of professional services provided by the office. Job Description Summary Graduate Assistant – Access, Connections, and Engagement ( ACE ) Office Division of Student Affairs – Marshall University The Graduate Assistant for the Access, Connections, and Engagement ( ACE ) Office supports programs, services, and initiatives that promote student success, active participation, and connection to the campus and surrounding community. Working closely with professional staff, the Graduate Assistant assists in planning, coordinating, and evaluating events, workshops, and outreach efforts that link students to campus resources, local opportunities, and networks that strengthen their academic and personal development. This role offers valuable hands-on experience in student affairs, program development, and student engagement while contributing to the ACE Office’s mission of fostering strong connections and enhancing the Marshall student experience. Responsibilities: Assist in planning, coordinating, and implementing ACE Office events, workshops, and activities. Support outreach efforts to connect students with campus resources and community opportunities. Maintain and update ACE Office communications, including email, flyers, and social media content. Collect and analyze data for program assessment and improvement. Mentor and guide undergraduate student staff and volunteers. Provide front-line support for students visiting the ACE Center, answering questions and connecting them to services. Collaborate with campus partners to enhance awareness of ACE Office programs. Assist with office organization, scheduling, and general administrative tasks. Represent the ACE Office at campus and community events as needed. Will be working 50% with Global Education Department Access Connections Engagement (ACE) - MU3504 Location MU - Marshall University Semester Fall Semester, Spring Semester Hours Per Week Full Time (20 hrs a week) Qualifications Required Qualifications Education Bachelor’s Degree seeking Master’s Degree Experience MUST BE ACCEPTED IN GRADUATE PROGRAM ; Office Administration experience preferred. Preferred Qualifications Education Experience Posting Detail Information Posting Number MU3124GA Open Date 08/03/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
