iatric Neurology patients in both inpatient and outpatient settings. Provide general pediatric neurology call coverage with other pediatric neurologists in a shared system. Active in physician and hospital outreach activities related to pediatric neurology. Participate in medical student and resident education, as well as research. All other appropriate duties as assigned by the chair of the Department of Neurology. Location MUSOM - Marshall University School of Medicine Salary Range Salary is commensurate with experience and internal equity Qualifications Must be able to perform all essential job duties as outlined in the job description. Required Qualifications Education A medical degree and completion of residency training in Neurology and a fellowship in Pediatric Neurology. Experience The ideal candidate(s) will have an interest in academic medicine with an emphasis on clinic-based practice. Must have a strong desire to teach and mentor medical students Preferred Qualifications Education Experience Posting Detail Information Posting Number MU1897F Open Date 08/21/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you completed all of the following:\r\nA medical degree and completion of residency training in Neurology and a fellowship in Pediatric Neurology? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
