    "https://marshall.peopleadmin.com/postings/32749": {
      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor- Obstetrics and Gynecology- Female Pelvic Medicine and Reconstructive Surgery",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor- Obstetrics and Gynecology- Female Pelvic Medicine and Reconstructive Surgery Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Assistant Professor- Obstetrics and Gynecology- Female Pelvic Medicine and Reconstructive Surgery Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Get to Know Us! Marshall University is a public comprehensive university with a rich history as one of the oldest institutions of higher learning in West Virginia. Founded in 1837 and named after Chief Justice John Marshall, definer of the Constitution, Marshall University advances the public good through innovative, accredited educational programs. We are located in downtown Huntington, West Virginia, with additional locations in South Charleston, Point Pleasant, Teays Valley and Beckley. Marshall University’s mission, inspired by our Vision and Creed, includes a commitment to: Offer a wide range of high quality, affordable, and accessible undergraduate, graduate, and professional education that prepares students to think, learn, work, and live in an evolving global society. Create opportunities and experiences to foster understanding and appreciation of the rich diversity of thought and culture. Maintain a dynamic intellectual, artistic, and cultural life by promoting and supporting research and creative activities by undergraduates, graduates, and faculty. Contribute to the quality of life of the community, region, and beyond through applied research, economic development, health care, and cultural enrichment. Cultivate the development of an inclusive, just, and equitable community. Come Meet Marshall and discover what it means to be part of the Marshall University family! Come join our Herd! We are committed to attracting and retaining quality faculty and staff. In doing so, Marshall University offers outstanding benefit packages to eligible employees only. (E-Class in the job posting). Marshall University Research Corporation ( MURC ) employees have different benefit options than those listed below. Work week is 37.5 hrs. A great highlight in December is that Marshall University employees receive almost two weeks off for Winter Break! Holidays – Employees receive 13 Paid Holidays Annual and Sick Leave – Classified Staff, Non-Classified Staff and 12-month Faculty earn up to 24 days of annual leave per year (max 360 hours) and up to 18 days of sick leave per year. ) Employee Leave Health Insurance – Marshall University offers health insurance through West Virginia Public Employees Insurance Agency ( PEIA ). There are seven (7) health benefit plans. Educational/Tuition Benefits – Marshall University provides tuition benefits to regular employees (after probationary period) and their dependent children. Retirement Plans – Marshall University offers retirement through Teachers Insurance and Annuity Association ( TIAA ). Full-time benefits eligible employees must participate in the mandated retirement plan (401(a)). Life Insurance – Basic term life insurance ($10,000) at no cost and may purchase optional life insurance coverage with pre-tax earnings. Wellness Programs – PEIA provides various care management programs and the Pathways to Wellness program. We are . . . Marshall! Position Information Banner Position Number 001469 Position Title Assistant Professor- Obstetrics and Gynecology- Female Pelvic Medicine and Reconstructive Surgery Classification Title Assistant Professor Department SOM-OB-GYN - MU9430 Job Description The School of Medicine Obstetrics and Gynecology department is seeking a full-time gynecologist with subspecialty certification in Female Pelvic Medicine and Reconstructive Surgery. The successful candidate will: Provide ambulatory and surgical care for women a variety of gynecologic conditions with a focus on pelvic support disorders and urinary incontinence. Provide direct clinical supervision of residents; Provide didactic instruction to residents; Provide student lectures, seminar, moderation and clinical teaching in conjunction with student curriculum devised by the Clerkship Director; Participate on the clinical research program develop on the department and facilitate recruitment of patients on an as needed basis; Provide direct patient care; Provide gynecologic care to women in the emergency department and inpatient consultation. Participate in other clinical activities of the department; Consult with Chair on any potential new OB/ GYN market opportunities; Participate in productivity and cost analysis projects; Work closely with the Curriculum committee of MUSOM to ensure compatibility of departmental goals and objectives with institutional goals and objectives; Explore new and innovative teaching techniques. Location MUSOM - Marshall University School of Medicine Salary Range Salary is commensurate with experience and internal equity Qualifications Must be able to perform all essential job duties as outlined in the job description. Required Qualifications Education MD or foreign equivalent Experience Completion of four year residency in obstetrics and gynecology and American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology Certification or active candidate required. Subspecialty certification in Female Pelvic Medicine and Reconstructive Surgery by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology Preferred Qualifications Education Experience Posting Detail Information Posting Number MU1405F Open Date 12/01/2023 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://marshall.peopleadmin.com/postings/32054": {
      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Quality Management Systems Specialist",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Quality Management Systems Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Quality Management Systems Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Banner Position Number R10796 Position Title Quality Management Systems Specialist Classification Title MURC-Misc Other Technicians Department RCBI Quality - RC15110Q Job Description The Marshall University Advanced Manufacturing Center ( MAMC ) is accepting resumes for a Quality Management Systems Specialist. Duties: The successful candidate will join a highly motivated, statewide team to provide training and consulting in quality and environmental management systems and continuous improvement, implement modern management practices, and perform other duties as assigned. Location OTHR - Other Off-Campus Location Salary Range $60.000 - $70,000 - salary is commensurate with education, experience, and internal equity Required Qualifications Education Associate’s Degree with equivalent experience is required. Experience · Three years’ experience in developing and implementing management systems to meet industry-specific requirements is required. Proficiency in flowcharting and statistical analysis software is required. · The ability to job shadow, document processes and develop job instructions is required. · Strong written and oral communications skills – as well as experience with group instruction – are essential. · Ability to successfully recruit companies for quality management services and perform outreach visits to industry is essential. The successful candidate must have the ability to work as part of a larger MAMC team. · Candidate is required to be proficient in MS Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, video conferencing, flowcharting, and statistical analysis software as well as use of audiovisual equipment. · A pre-employment background check is required. · Overnight travel is occasionally required . Preferred Qualifications Education Bachelor’s Degree Experience · Extensive knowledge of manufacturing quality and environmental management systems based on ISO 9000, and other industry-specific standards. · Experience in metrology. · Experience with energy assessments and/or audits. · Curriculum development for in-person and virtual training using various presentation software and delivery platforms. Professional certifications are preferred Posting Detail Information Posting Number MR0867 Open Date 06/02/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://marshall.peopleadmin.com/postings/32865": {
      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Vice Dean of Healthy Aging Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Vice Dean of Healthy Aging Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Get to Know Us! Marshall University is a public comprehensive university with a rich history as one of the oldest institutions of higher learning in West Virginia. Founded in 1837 and named after Chief Justice John Marshall, definer of the Constitution, Marshall University advances the public good through innovative, accredited educational programs. We are located in downtown Huntington, West Virginia, with additional locations in South Charleston, Point Pleasant, Teays Valley and Beckley. Marshall University’s mission, inspired by our Vision and Creed, includes a commitment to: Offer a wide range of high quality, affordable, and accessible undergraduate, graduate, and professional education that prepares students to think, learn, work, and live in an evolving global society. Create opportunities and experiences to foster understanding and appreciation of the rich diversity of thought and culture. Maintain a dynamic intellectual, artistic, and cultural life by promoting and supporting research and creative activities by undergraduates, graduates, and faculty. Contribute to the quality of life of the community, region, and beyond through applied research, economic development, health care, and cultural enrichment. Cultivate the development of an inclusive, just, and equitable community. Come Meet Marshall and discover what it means to be part of the Marshall University family! Come join our Herd! We are committed to attracting and retaining quality faculty and staff. In doing so, Marshall University offers outstanding benefit packages to eligible employees only. (E-Class in the job posting). Marshall University Research Corporation ( MURC ) employees have different benefit options than those listed below. Work week is 37.5 hrs. A great highlight in December is that Marshall University employees receive almost two weeks off for Winter Break! Holidays – Employees receive 13 Paid Holidays Annual and Sick Leave – Classified Staff, Non-Classified Staff and 12-month Faculty earn up to 24 days of annual leave per year (max 360 hours) and up to 18 days of sick leave per year. ) Employee Leave Health Insurance – Marshall University offers health insurance through West Virginia Public Employees Insurance Agency ( PEIA ). There are seven (7) health benefit plans. Educational/Tuition Benefits – Marshall University provides tuition benefits to regular employees (after probationary period) and their dependent children. Retirement Plans – Marshall University offers retirement through Teachers Insurance and Annuity Association ( TIAA ). Full-time benefits eligible employees must participate in the mandated retirement plan (401(a)). Life Insurance – Basic term life insurance ($10,000) at no cost and may purchase optional life insurance coverage with pre-tax earnings. Wellness Programs – PEIA provides various care management programs and the Pathways to Wellness program. We are . . . Marshall! Position Information Banner Position Number 001845 Position Title Vice Dean of Healthy Aging Classification Title Associate Dean (Faculty) Department SOM-VP Health Science/Dean - MU9000 Job Description Position Overview The Joan C. Edwards School of Medicine ( JCESOM ) at Marshall University, in partnership with Marshall Health Network ( MHN ), seeks an accomplished and visionary physician (MD/DO) or scientist (PhD) to serve as the Vice Dean of Healthy Aging . This senior leadership role will advance a comprehensive strategy to improve health outcomes, research, education, and community engagement focused on aging populations across Appalachia and beyond. The Vice Dean will lead the development of innovative clinical, educational, and research initiatives that promote healthy aging, address the complexities of geriatric care, and position Marshall as a national leader in aging and longevity science. Key Responsibilities: Strategic Leadership Develop and execute a system-wide vision and strategic plan for healthy aging across Marshall University aligned with the mission MHN . Establish Marshall as a regional and national leader in gerontology and healthy aging initiatives. Collaborate with executive leadership to integrate aging-focused priorities across clinical care, research, and education. Clinical Integration Partner with clinical departments to enhance geriatric care delivery models, including primary care, specialty care, and community-based services. Support development of innovative care models addressing chronic disease, frailty, cognitive decline, and social determinants of health. Promote interdisciplinary approaches to care for older adults. Research Development Expand and support a robust portfolio of aging-related research, including translational, clinical, and population health studies. Foster collaborations across departments, institutions, and external partners. Pursue federal, state, and philanthropic funding opportunities focused on aging and longevity. Education, Training & Fellowship Oversight Provide strategic and operational oversight of the Gerontology/Geriatrics Fellowship Program , ensuring program excellence, accreditation compliance, and alignment with institutional priorities. Collaborate with program leadership to enhance curriculum development, clinical training experiences, and scholarly activity. Support recruitment, mentorship, and career development of fellows pursuing careers in geriatrics and aging-related disciplines. Advance geriatric education across undergraduate medical education, graduate medical education, and continuing professional development. Develop and expand training pathways, including new fellowships or certificates in aging-related fields. Community Engagement & Outreach Strengthen partnerships with community organizations, long-term care facilities, and public health entities. Lead initiatives addressing rural aging populations and health disparities in Appalachia. Promote programs that support aging in place, caregiver support, and population health Personal Attributes: Visionary and strategic thinker with a passion for improving the lives of older adults. Collaborative leader with the ability to engage diverse stakeholders. Strong communication and relationship-building skills. Commitment to the mission of academic medicine and service to underserved populations. Reporting Structure: The Vice Dean of Healthy Aging will report to the Dean of the Joan C. Edwards School of Medicine. The successful candidate will also have a faculty appointment in the appropriate department and have a dotted line to that respective department chair. The successful candidate will work closely with executive leadership across Marshall University and Marshall Health Network. Opportunity: This is a unique opportunity to shape the future of aging care and research in a region with significant need and opportunity. The successful candidate will play a pivotal role in advancing innovative solutions that improve longevity, quality of life, and health equity for aging populations. Application Process: Qualified candidates should submit a CV and a letter of interest outlining their vision for advancing healthy aging initiatives at Marshall University. Marshall University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. Location MUSOM - Marshall University School of Medicine Salary Range Salary is  commensurate with education and experience Qualifications Must be able to perform all essential job duties as outlined in the job description. Required Qualifications Education MD, DO, and/or PhD in a relevant field. Experience Demonstrated leadership experience in academic medicine, healthcare administration, or research. Strong record of scholarship, funding, and/or program development in aging-related fields. Experience working in interdisciplinary and collaborative environments. Preferred Qualifications Education Board certification in Geriatric Medicine or Gerontology (for physician candidates). Experience Established research program focused on aging, geriatrics, or related disciplines (for PhD candidates). Experience in rural health, population health, or health system transformation. National recognition in the field of aging, geriatrics, or gerontology. Posting Detail Information Posting Number MU1889F Open Date 08/04/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a MD, DO, and/or PhD in a relevant field? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://marshall.peopleadmin.com/postings/29176": {
      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Surgery- Trauma Surgeon",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Surgery- Trauma Surgeon Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Assistant Professor of Surgery- Trauma Surgeon Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Get to Know Us! Marshall University is a public comprehensive university with a rich history as one of the oldest institutions of higher learning in West Virginia. Founded in 1837 and named after Chief Justice John Marshall, definer of the Constitution, Marshall University advances the public good through innovative, accredited educational programs. We are located in downtown Huntington, West Virginia, with additional locations in South Charleston, Point Pleasant, Teays Valley and Beckley. Marshall University’s mission, inspired by our Vision and Creed, includes a commitment to: Offer a wide range of high quality, affordable, and accessible undergraduate, graduate, and professional education that prepares students to think, learn, work, and live in an evolving global society. Create opportunities and experiences to foster understanding and appreciation of the rich diversity of thought and culture. Maintain a dynamic intellectual, artistic, and cultural life by promoting and supporting research and creative activities by undergraduates, graduates, and faculty. Contribute to the quality of life of the community, region, and beyond through applied research, economic development, health care, and cultural enrichment. Cultivate the development of an inclusive, just, and equitable community. Come Meet Marshall and discover what it means to be part of the Marshall University family! Come join our Herd! We are committed to attracting and retaining quality faculty and staff. In doing so, Marshall University offers outstanding benefit packages to eligible employees only. (E-Class in the job posting). Marshall University Research Corporation ( MURC ) employees have different benefit options than those listed below. Work week is 37.5 hrs. A great highlight in December is that Marshall University employees receive almost two weeks off for Winter Break! Holidays – Employees receive 13 Paid Holidays Annual and Sick Leave – Classified Staff, Non-Classified Staff and 12-month Faculty earn up to 24 days of annual leave per year (max 360 hours) and up to 18 days of sick leave per year. ) Employee Leave Health Insurance – Marshall University offers health insurance through West Virginia Public Employees Insurance Agency ( PEIA ). There are seven (7) health benefit plans. Educational/Tuition Benefits – Marshall University provides tuition benefits to regular employees (after probationary period) and their dependent children. Retirement Plans – Marshall University offers retirement through Teachers Insurance and Annuity Association ( TIAA ). Full-time benefits eligible employees must participate in the mandated retirement plan (401(a)). Life Insurance – Basic term life insurance ($10,000) at no cost and may purchase optional life insurance coverage with pre-tax earnings. Wellness Programs – PEIA provides various care management programs and the Pathways to Wellness program. We are . . . Marshall! Position Information Banner Position Number 000492 Position Title Assistant Professor of Surgery- Trauma Surgeon Classification Title Assistant Professor Department SOM-Surgery - MU9450 Job Description Trauma Surgeon (Assistant Professor of Surgery): Provide surgical care including trauma surgical care to patients as a faculty/attending physician at the facility in Cabell County, WV. In affiliation w/ Marshall University, duties include, to provide supervision & clinical instruction to medical students & residents in general surgery, trauma surgery & related areas. Participate in rounds & present at one or more Medical Grand Rounds per year. SOC Code 25-1071 5% allocation of duties F/T position w/ University Physicians & Surgeons Inc. d/b/a Marshall Health. CV to J. Gerlach to gerlach8@marshall.edu Location MUSOM - Marshall University School of Medicine Salary Range Salary is commensurate with experience and internal equity Qualifications Must be able to perform all essential job duties as outlined in the job description. Required Qualifications Education MD or professional equivalent degree in Medicine Experience BC or BE in Surgery; BC/BE in Trauma Surgery or Surgical Critical Care; WV Medical. License eligibility Preferred Qualifications Education Experience Posting Detail Information Posting Number MU1678F Open Date 05/08/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
