    "https://marshall.peopleadmin.com/postings/32572": {
      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Youth Navigator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Youth Navigator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Banner Position Number R10915 Position Title Youth Navigator Classification Title MURC-Other Bus Operations Spec Department Center of Excellence for Recovery - RC1524 Job Description Position Summary: The Navigator is responsible for providing comprehensive case management, care coordination, outreach, and navigation services to transition-age youth and young adults (ages 16–26). The Youth Navigator serves as a trusted partner, helping participants identify strengths, overcome barriers, and access coordinated services that promote health, education, employment, housing stability, behavioral health, and overall well-being.The Youth Navigator will build collaborative relationships with community providers, educational institutions, workforce partners, healthcare organizations, and social service agencies to ensure participants receive timely, coordinated, and person-centered care. This position utilizes trauma-informed, culturally responsive, and youth-driven practices to empower young adults toward self-sufficiency and long-term success. Essential Functions Conduct outreach and engagement activities to identify and connect with eligible youth and young adults through schools, community organizations, healthcare providers, workforce partners, and community events. Complete participant intake, screening, strengths-based assessments, and eligibility determination for COE services. Develop individualized service and goal plans in collaboration with participants, incorporating education, employment, health, behavioral health, housing, transportation, and other supportive service needs. Provide ongoing care coordination through regular meetings, follow-up contacts, home or community visits (as appropriate), and progress monitoring. Serve as the primary point of contact for participants, providing guidance, advocacy, encouragement, and system navigation throughout their participation in the COE . Coordinate referrals and facilitate access to internal and external resources, ensuring warm handoffs and continuity of care. Build and maintain collaborative partnerships with community agencies, educational institutions, healthcare providers, behavioral health organizations, employers, and workforce development programs. Monitor participant progress toward established goals and modify service plans as needed. Assist participants with crisis intervention, problem-solving, and barrier reduction while maintaining appropriate professional boundaries. Maintain accurate, timely, and confidential participant records, case notes, assessments, referrals, and outcomes in accordance with agency policies and funding requirements. Collect program data and assist with quality improvement initiatives, grant reporting, and performance outcome measures. Participate in multidisciplinary team meetings, case conferences, trainings, and community collaborative meetings. Represent the Center of Excellence at outreach events, networking opportunities, and community presentations. Maintain knowledge of local resources, emerging community needs, and best practices in youth engagement and care coordination. Perform other duties as assigned. Location OTHR - Other Off-Campus Location Salary Range $40,000 Salary is commensurate with education, experience and internal equity Required Qualifications Education Bachelor’s degree in Social Work, Human Services, Psychology, Counseling, Public Health, Criminal Justice, Education, or a closely related field. Experience One – two years of experience in case management, care coordination, youth services, behavioral health, workforce development, or community-based human services preferred. Experience working with transition-age youth (16–26), underserved populations, or individuals experiencing barriers to education, employment, housing, or healthcare preferred Preferred Qualifications Education Experience Posting Detail Information Posting Number MR0886 Open Date 07/29/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor's degree in Social Work, Human Services, Psychology, Counseling, Public Health, Criminal Justice, Education, or a closely related field? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
