es have different benefit options than those listed below. Work week is 37.5 hrs. A great highlight in December is that Marshall University employees receive almost two weeks off for Winter Break! Holidays – Employees receive 13 Paid Holidays Annual and Sick Leave – Classified Staff, Non-Classified Staff and 12-month Faculty earn up to 24 days of annual leave per year (max 360 hours) and up to 18 days of sick leave per year. ) Employee Leave Health Insurance – Marshall University offers health insurance through West Virginia Public Employees Insurance Agency ( PEIA ). There are seven (7) health benefit plans. Educational/Tuition Benefits – Marshall University provides tuition benefits to regular employees (after probationary period) and their dependent children. Retirement Plans – Marshall University offers retirement through Teachers Insurance and Annuity Association ( TIAA ). Full-time benefits eligible employees must participate in the mandated retirement plan (401(a)). Life Insurance – Basic term life insurance ($10,000) at no cost and may purchase optional life insurance coverage with pre-tax earnings. Wellness Programs – PEIA provides various care management programs and the Pathways to Wellness program. We are . . . Marshall! Position Information Banner Position Number 000413 Position Title Assistant Professor Classification Title Assistant Professor Department COHP-Nursing - MU9510 Job Description The School of Nursing in the College of Health Professions has an opening for a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track Assistant Professor. Position available August 2026. Responsible for the accreditation of the MSN program. Curriculum development, revision, and evaluation. Active engagement in student recruitment, admission, and progression. Location MU - Marshall University Salary Range Salary is commensurate upon education, experience and internal equity Qualifications Must be able to perform all essential job duties as outlined in the job description. Required Qualifications Education Required – Terminal Degree (Doctoral Degree) Master of Science in Nursing from an accredited nursing program. Required: FNP Certification. Current West Virginia license or a license from a Compact state or ability to obtain licenses prior to the start of contract. Experience At least three years practicing in the Advance Practice role. Cross-cultural communication skills, with multicultural sensitivity and experience interacting effectively with diverse students, faculty, and staff desire. Required: At least two years’ experience teaching at the graduate level. Preferred Qualifications Education Experience Posting Detail Information Posting Number MU1804F Open Date 03/26/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Terminal Degree (Doctoral Degree) Master of Science in Nursing from an accredited nursing program? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter CV or Resume Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
