    "https://marshall.peopleadmin.com/postings/32268": {
      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant - Women&#39;s Center (Part-time)",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant - Women&#39;s Center (Part-time) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Graduate Assistant - Women's Center (Part-time) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Graduate Assistant - Women's Center (Part-time) Description of GA Assignment GA: Clinical Practice - The department will assign you to various tasks that will require you to provide professional service to MU students, clients of a MU Clinic, or other individuals in need of professional services provided by the office. Job Description Summary The Women’s Center serves as Marshall University’s central resource for women and femme-identifying students, faculty, and staff. The Center strives to foster allyship around issues of gender and is dedicated to advancing equity and inclusion at Marshall through education, advocacy, resource connection, and leadership development. The Women’s Center Graduate Assistant reports directly to the Women’s Center Program Coordinator. The Center includes a Program Coordinator, Graduate Assistant, Undergraduate Student Assistants, and Student Volunteers and Interns. All staff members collaborate to facilitate education, awareness, networking, and advocacy services for the campus community. Primary responsibilities reflect the strengths and experience of the individual team members. • Staff the Women’s Center during regular office hours and provide student support services. • Assist with planning and implementing leadership opportunities and recognition, including the annual Women of Marshall Awards. • Assist with the assessment and evaluation of Center programs and services. • Assist and implement development and delivery of educational programming to UNI 100 classes, residence halls, student organizations, and university employees regarding self-esteem & body image, gender in the media, healthy masculinity, career preparation, leadership skills, allyship, advocacy training, and reproductive resources. • Assist with organizing and implementing awareness activities and events throughout the year, including Salary Negotiation Workshops, Reproductive and Sexual Health programs, Women’s Equality Day, and Women’s History Month events. • Collaborate with various campus and community entities to facilitate outreach events, networking opportunities, and resource connections for students. • Work with the Program Coordinator to recruit, train, and supervise Student Volunteers and Peer Educators. • Maintain thorough and accurate documentation for Center programming and outreach. • Enhance the Center’s social media outreach on a variety of platforms and maintain the website as needed. • Participate in ongoing training and professional development opportunitie Department Women & Gender Center - MU3020 Location MU - Marshall University Semester Fall Semester Hours Per Week Part Time (10 hrs a week) Qualifications Required Qualifications Education Bachelor’s Degree Experience Must be able to perform all essential job duties as outlined in the job description. Preferred Qualifications Education Experience Posting Detail Information Posting Number MU3063GA Open Date 06/30/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a fully admitted graduate student? Yes No * Do you have a valid Drivers License? Yes No * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree in a human services field? Yes No * Describe your prior experiences related to the duties of this position. (Open Ended Question) * Tell us about your track record with managing a grant-funded project or program and meeting or exceeding objectives, including managing budgets and tracking financial expenditures, gathering data, compiling information, and preparing reports. (Open Ended Question) * Have you had any experience working with the LGBTQ+ community? (Open Ended Question) * Are you able to work evenings, weekends, and holidays to fulfill the job responsibilities? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Course Syllabi Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://marshall.peopleadmin.com/postings/31515": {
      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant - 5 Positions Available",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant - 5 Positions Available Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Graduate Assistant - 5 Positions Available Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Graduate Assistant - 5 Positions Available Description of GA Assignment GA: Clinical Practice - The department will assign you to various tasks that will require you to provide professional service to MU students, clients of a MU Clinic, or other individuals in need of professional services provided by the office. Job Description Summary Summer Semester 2026 Graduate Assistants hired with the College Program for Students with ASD work as mentors for college students with ASD in academic, social, and independent living development areas. Time is spent directly supporting participating students as they navigate the college environment. Mentors are required to oversee evening study halls, help assist in test proctoring, as well as plan and participate in various social activities throughout the semester. This role requires that mentors regularly communicate and meet with their students and staff Support Specialists. Mentors are expected to attend any staff training that occurs during the semester. Department ASD College Program - MU2432 Location MU - Marshall University Semester Summer Semester Hours Per Week Full Time (20 hrs a week) Qualifications Required Qualifications Education Bachelor’s degree required and enrolled full time in a master’s program. Experience Experience working with individuals diagnosed with ASD in a higher education setting preferred. Preferred Qualifications Education Experience Posting Detail Information Posting Number MU2992GA Open Date 03/26/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
