      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Cardiovascular Medicine- Advanced Heart Failure Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Assistant Professor of Cardiovascular Medicine- Advanced Heart Failure Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Get to Know Us! Marshall University is a public comprehensive university with a rich history as one of the oldest institutions of higher learning in West Virginia. Founded in 1837 and named after Chief Justice John Marshall, definer of the Constitution, Marshall University advances the public good through innovative, accredited educational programs. We are located in downtown Huntington, West Virginia, with additional locations in South Charleston, Point Pleasant, Teays Valley and Beckley. Marshall University’s mission, inspired by our Vision and Creed, includes a commitment to: Offer a wide range of high quality, affordable, and accessible undergraduate, graduate, and professional education that prepares students to think, learn, work, and live in an evolving global society. Create opportunities and experiences to foster understanding and appreciation of the rich diversity of thought and culture. Maintain a dynamic intellectual, artistic, and cultural life by promoting and supporting research and creative activities by undergraduates, graduates, and faculty. Contribute to the quality of life of the community, region, and beyond through applied research, economic development, health care, and cultural enrichment. Cultivate the development of an inclusive, just, and equitable community. Come Meet Marshall and discover what it means to be part of the Marshall University family! Come join our Herd! We are committed to attracting and retaining quality faculty and staff. In doing so, Marshall University offers outstanding benefit packages to eligible employees only. (E-Class in the job posting). Marshall University Research Corporation ( MURC ) employees have different benefit options than those listed below. Work week is 37.5 hrs. A great highlight in December is that Marshall University employees receive almost two weeks off for Winter Break! Holidays – Employees receive 13 Paid Holidays Annual and Sick Leave – Classified Staff, Non-Classified Staff and 12-month Faculty earn up to 24 days of annual leave per year (max 360 hours) and up to 18 days of sick leave per year. ) Employee Leave Health Insurance – Marshall University offers health insurance through West Virginia Public Employees Insurance Agency ( PEIA ). There are seven (7) health benefit plans. Educational/Tuition Benefits – Marshall University provides tuition benefits to regular employees (after probationary period) and their dependent children. Retirement Plans – Marshall University offers retirement through Teachers Insurance and Annuity Association ( TIAA ). Full-time benefits eligible employees must participate in the mandated retirement plan (401(a)). Life Insurance – Basic term life insurance ($10,000) at no cost and may purchase optional life insurance coverage with pre-tax earnings. Wellness Programs – PEIA provides various care management programs and the Pathways to Wellness program. We are . . . Marshall! Position Information Banner Position Number 002335 Position Title Assistant Professor of Cardiovascular Medicine- Advanced Heart Failure Specialist Classification Title Assistant Professor Department SOM-Cardiovascular Services - MU9452 Job Description Position Summary The Marshall University Joan C. Edwards School of Medicine’s Department of Cardiovascular Services is seeking a board-certified/board-eligible Advanced Heart Failure Cardiologist to join our growing faculty. The ideal candidate will bring expertise in the diagnosis and management of complex heart failure, including pre- and post-transplant care, mechanical circulatory support, and advanced therapies. This role is part of a dynamic and expanding academic cardiology program in a collegial, team-based environment. Faculty physicians enjoy access to state-of-the-art facilities and strong institutional support for both clinical and academic growth. This position does not involve transplant or LVAD implantation, as these services are referred to external centers. This appointment is open at the Assistant or Associate Professor level on a clinical track, depending on the candidate’s qualifications and interests. Responsibilities Provide comprehensive care for patients with advanced heart failure, including those requiring mechanical circulatory support or transplant evaluation. Participate in the development and advancement of the Advanced Heart Failure program, working closely with multidisciplinary teams. Serve as attending physician at one primary site, with coverage rotating among two hospitals and satellite clinics. Participate in inpatient rounding every 6th weekend, with support from cardiology fellows (no year-round call requirement). Teach and mentor general cardiology fellows, residents, and medical students in both formal and informal settings. Engage in scholarly activity including quality improvement initiatives, clinical research, and collaboration with Marshall’s translational and biomedical sciences programs. Additional Information This position qualifies for J-1 visa sponsorship Faculty are supported by an ACGME -approved cardiology fellowship program and advanced cardiovascular imaging programs Marshall Health is part of a thriving health system with two major hospital partners and an expanding regional network Marshall University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages all qualified individuals to apply. Marshall University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages all qualified individuals to apply Location MUSOM - Marshall University School of Medicine Salary Range Commensurate with qualifications and experience Qualifications Must be able to perform all essential job duties as outlined in the job description. Required Qualifications Education MD or DO (or foreign equivalent) Experience Successful completion of an ACGME -accredited Cardiovascular Disease fellowship and an Advanced Heart Failure and Transplant Cardiology fellowship Board Certified in Cardiovascular Disease • Board Eligible in Advanced Heart Failure and Transplant Cardiology Must hold or be eligible for a full and unrestricted West Virginia medical license at the time of employment Must be able to perform all essential duties as outlined in the position Must meet qualifications for faculty appointment at the Marshall University Joan C. Edwards School of Medicine Preferred Qualifications Education Experience Posting Detail Information Posting Number MU1718F Open Date 08/04/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a MD or DO (or foreign equivalent)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
