    "https://marshall.peopleadmin.com/postings/31609": {
      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant-Part time (10 hours per week)  1 positions available",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant-Part time (10 hours per week)  1 positions available Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Graduate Assistant-Part time (10 hours per week)  1 positions available Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Graduate Assistant-Part time (10 hours per week)  1 positions available Description of GA Assignment GA: Faculty Support - Assist faculty, services may include tasks as supervising laboratories under their supervision; grading quizzes, homework, and other projects; and assist with other course and research related duties as assigned. Job Description Summary • Provide one-on-one academic tutoring to teach and reteach concepts to H.E.L.P. students • Offer assistance with developing study strategies • Work with students to develop a plan that fits the student’s individual needs • Assist students in developing a schedule for study sessions • Clarify/augment student notes from lecture • Teach concepts using multi-sensory techniques to maximize student understanding and recall • Teach organization and time managements skills • Monitor students’ progress through communication with students and professors • Send notification to professors regarding students’ with disabilities and accommodations • Organize and facilitate testing accommodations according to students’ diagnosis for compliance with Americans with Disabilities Act and Vocational Rehabilitation Act • Proctor exams under supervision • Maintain student attendance records • Notify students and parents regarding students’ absences from tutoring sessions • Write End of Semester Reports for each student • Participate in scheduled tutor training and development sessions Department H.E.L.P. Program - MUHR01 Location MU - Marshall University Semester Fall Semester Hours Per Week Part Time (10 hrs a week) Qualifications Required Qualifications Education Bachelor’s Degree Experience Must be able to perform duties as described in the job description. Preferred Qualifications Education Bachelor’s Degree Experience Tutoring Posting Detail Information Posting Number MU3000GA Open Date 04/01/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
