    "https://marshall.peopleadmin.com/postings/32776": {
      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Grants Management/ Administrative Specialist",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Grants Management/ Administrative Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Grants Management/ Administrative Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Banner Position Number R10920 Position Title Grants Management/ Administrative Specialist Classification Title MURC-Secretary/Admin Assistant Department SOM-BioMedical Science - RC5130 Job Description The West Virginia-IDeA Network of Biomedical Research Excellence (WV- INBRE ) invites applications for a Grants Administrator.Salary will be commensurate with relevant skills and experience and funded through a grant from National Institutes of Health. Duties will include, but are not limited to, the following: (1) management of the WV- INBRE grant budget; (2) working with the leadership team to support WV-INBRE’s statewide, multi-institutional research program; (3) provision of daily support, guidance, and assistance to faculty and students involved in WV- INBRE activities in the summer research programs; (4) serving as a WV- INBRE network administrator which involves regular contact with faculty and staff at universities and colleges throughout the state; (5) participating in periodic employee training provided through Marshall University and the Marshall University Research Corporation (this includes IT skills, financial processes, grant administration and research administration practices); (6) applying knowledge of state and federal regulations, agency policy and other requirements that affect grant program administration; (7) analyzing and evaluating methods to identify and resolve grant administration and compliance issues; and (8) performing other grant related responsibilities which include, but are not limited to purchasing, processing travel requests, invoicing, assisting with organization of committee meetings and coordinating with the Summer Research Director on the implementation of our summer research program and symposium. The position is open until filled; a background check is required. Marshall University is an EEO /AA. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Preference will be given to US Citizens and Permanent Residents. Location MURC - Marshall University Research Corporation Salary Range Salary is commensurate with experience and internal equity Required Qualifications Education The minimum requirement is a bachelor’s degree preferably in Business, Biological Sciences or Biomedical Sciences. Experience Experience working with MS Excel is required Candidates must also possess excellent interpersonal and communication (oral and written) skills, have demonstrated good time management and adept at handling multiple grant-related tasks Preferred Qualifications Education Experience We will prefer applicants with prior experience in grants management, using Microsoft Office, Zoom, One Drive and similar systems, and familiarity with Banner or similar financial reporting systems. Experience with federal grant applications highly desirable. Posting Detail Information Posting Number MR0892 Open Date 08/21/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a  bachelor’s degree or higher? Yes No * Are you adept at handling multiple Grant-related tasks? Yes No * Do you have strong Microsoft EXCEL skills? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://marshall.peopleadmin.com/postings/30042": {
      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor-  Obstetrics and Gynecology- Reproductive Endocrinology/Infertility",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor-  Obstetrics and Gynecology- Reproductive Endocrinology/Infertility Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Assistant Professor-  Obstetrics and Gynecology- Reproductive Endocrinology/Infertility Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Get to Know Us! Marshall University is a public comprehensive university with a rich history as one of the oldest institutions of higher learning in West Virginia. Founded in 1837 and named after Chief Justice John Marshall, definer of the Constitution, Marshall University advances the public good through innovative, accredited educational programs. We are located in downtown Huntington, West Virginia, with additional locations in South Charleston, Point Pleasant, Teays Valley and Beckley. Marshall University’s mission, inspired by our Vision and Creed, includes a commitment to: Offer a wide range of high quality, affordable, and accessible undergraduate, graduate, and professional education that prepares students to think, learn, work, and live in an evolving global society. Create opportunities and experiences to foster understanding and appreciation of the rich diversity of thought and culture. Maintain a dynamic intellectual, artistic, and cultural life by promoting and supporting research and creative activities by undergraduates, graduates, and faculty. Contribute to the quality of life of the community, region, and beyond through applied research, economic development, health care, and cultural enrichment. Cultivate the development of an inclusive, just, and equitable community. Come Meet Marshall and discover what it means to be part of the Marshall University family! Come join our Herd! We are committed to attracting and retaining quality faculty and staff. In doing so, Marshall University offers outstanding benefit packages to eligible employees only. (E-Class in the job posting). Marshall University Research Corporation ( MURC ) employees have different benefit options than those listed below. Work week is 37.5 hrs. A great highlight in December is that Marshall University employees receive almost two weeks off for Winter Break! Holidays – Employees receive 13 Paid Holidays Annual and Sick Leave – Classified Staff, Non-Classified Staff and 12-month Faculty earn up to 24 days of annual leave per year (max 360 hours) and up to 18 days of sick leave per year. ) Employee Leave Health Insurance – Marshall University offers health insurance through West Virginia Public Employees Insurance Agency ( PEIA ). There are seven (7) health benefit plans. Educational/Tuition Benefits – Marshall University provides tuition benefits to regular employees (after probationary period) and their dependent children. Retirement Plans – Marshall University offers retirement through Teachers Insurance and Annuity Association ( TIAA ). Full-time benefits eligible employees must participate in the mandated retirement plan (401(a)). Life Insurance – Basic term life insurance ($10,000) at no cost and may purchase optional life insurance coverage with pre-tax earnings. Wellness Programs – PEIA provides various care management programs and the Pathways to Wellness program. We are . . . Marshall! Position Information Banner Position Number 001847 Position Title Assistant Professor-  Obstetrics and Gynecology- Reproductive Endocrinology/Infertility Classification Title Assistant Professor Department SOM-OB-GYN - MU9430 Job Description The School of Medicine Obstetrics and Gynecology department is seeking a full-time gynecologist with a subspecialty certification in Reproductive Endocrinology and Infertility The successful candidate will: Provide ambulatory and surgical care for women with a focus on reproductive and endocrine system disorders that affect fertility including in vitro fertilization. Provide direct clinical supervision of residents; Provide didactic instruction to residents; Provide student lectures, seminar, moderation and clinical teaching in conjunction with student curriculum devised by the Clerkship Director; Participate on the clinical research program develop on the department and facilitate recruitment of patients on an as needed basis; Provide direct patient care; Participate in other clinical activities of the department; Consult with Chair on any potential new OB/ GYN market opportunities; Participate in productivity and cost analysis projects; Work closely with the Curriculum committee of MUSOM to ensure compatibility of departmental goals and objectives with institutional goals and objectives; Explore new and innovative teaching techniques. Location MUSOM - Marshall University School of Medicine Salary Range Salary is commensurate with experience and internal equity Qualifications Must be able to perform all essential job duties as outlined in the job description. Required Qualifications Education MD or equivalent Experience Completion of four-year residency in obstetrics and gynecology and American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology Certification or active candidate required. Subspecialty certification in Reproductive Endocrinology and Infertility by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology. Preferred Qualifications Education Experience Posting Detail Information Posting Number MU1721F Open Date 08/07/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have a Doctor of Medicine (MD or equivalent) from an accredited institution? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://marshall.peopleadmin.com/postings/32657": {
      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Program Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Program Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Get to Know Us! Marshall University is a public comprehensive university with a rich history as one of the oldest institutions of higher learning in West Virginia. Founded in 1837 and named after Chief Justice John Marshall, definer of the Constitution, Marshall University advances the public good through innovative, accredited educational programs. We are located in downtown Huntington, West Virginia, with additional locations in South Charleston, Point Pleasant, Teays Valley and Beckley. Marshall University’s mission, inspired by our Vision and Creed, includes a commitment to: Offer a wide range of high quality, affordable, and accessible undergraduate, graduate, and professional education that prepares students to think, learn, work, and live in an evolving global society. Create opportunities and experiences to foster understanding and appreciation of the rich diversity of thought and culture. Maintain a dynamic intellectual, artistic, and cultural life by promoting and supporting research and creative activities by undergraduates, graduates, and faculty. Contribute to the quality of life of the community, region, and beyond through applied research, economic development, health care, and cultural enrichment. Cultivate the development of an inclusive, just, and equitable community. Come Meet Marshall and discover what it means to be part of the Marshall University family! Come join our Herd! We are committed to attracting and retaining quality faculty and staff. In doing so, Marshall University offers outstanding benefit packages to eligible employees only. (E-Class in the job posting). Marshall University Research Corporation ( MURC ) employees have different benefit options than those listed below. Work week is 37.5 hrs. A great highlight in December is that Marshall University employees receive almost two weeks off for Winter Break! Holidays – Employees receive 13 Paid Holidays Annual and Sick Leave – Classified Staff, Non-Classified Staff and 12-month Faculty earn up to 24 days of annual leave per year (max 360 hours) and up to 18 days of sick leave per year. ) Employee Leave Health Insurance – Marshall University offers health insurance through West Virginia Public Employees Insurance Agency ( PEIA ). There are seven (7) health benefit plans. Educational/Tuition Benefits – Marshall University provides tuition benefits to regular employees (after probationary period) and their dependent children. Retirement Plans – Marshall University offers retirement through Teachers Insurance and Annuity Association ( TIAA ). Full-time benefits eligible employees must participate in the mandated retirement plan (401(a)). Life Insurance – Basic term life insurance ($10,000) at no cost and may purchase optional life insurance coverage with pre-tax earnings. Wellness Programs – PEIA provides various care management programs and the Pathways to Wellness program. We are . . . Marshall! Position Information Position Title Program Coordinator Banner Position Number 000816 E-Class CX - Class Exempt FT - .53 or > Department SOM-Med School Student Affairs - MU9252 Job Description The Program Coordinator within the Office of Student Affairs plays a critical role in ensuring the efficient and effective functioning of daily business operations. This position serves as the linchpin for coordinating a range of administrative activities, procurement processes, event planning, budget oversight, and database management. With a focus on maintaining seamless operations, the Program Coordinator collaborates closely with the Associate Dean of Student Affairs, the Director of Student Affairs , the Assistant Director of Student Financial Assistance, and the Assistant Director of Leadership Development and Wellness. This position is essential to the overall success of the department and the Joan C. Edwards School of Medicine. Job responsibilities: Manage the daily business operations for the Office of Student Affairs and serve as the point of contact for visitors Provides backup and support for the Office of Student Affairs Facilitate the creation, review, and processing of purchase orders and PARs Manage the purchasing, requisition, and Marketplace processes for the Office of Student Affairs Manage Student and Academic Affairs budgets and track expenditures Maintain up-to-date student information databases Oversee student lounges and address concerns as they arise Oversee and coordinate and oversee logistics, planning, and execution of student School of Medicine events Oversee the Astra room reservation system Manage, compile, and analyze on post-event surveys Development, distribution, and conducting initial analysis of online surveys Analyze and report on student outcome measures Responsible for coordinating travel arrangements for students, faculty, and staff Manage the distribution of parking permits and other needed student items Administer the organization, communication and collection of funds for student group packages for medical board exam prep Administrative support contact for student organizations Performs all other duties as assigned Salary Range $38,722 - $44,531  Salary is commensurate on education, experience, and internal equity Salary Type Salary Time Type Full-Time Work Location MUSOM - Marshall University School of Medicine Qualifications Must be able to perform all essential job duties as outlined in the job description. Required Qualifications Education Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration or a related field Experience Minimum two years or more of relevant work experience Preferred Qualifications Education Master’s degree in Business Administration or a related field Experience Knowledge of student affairs function; Banner experience Posting Detail Information Posting Number MU1280E Open Date 08/07/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor's degree in Business Administration or a related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum two years or more of relevant work experience? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
