    "https://marshall.peopleadmin.com/postings/32711": {
      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | C&amp;I Full-Time Faculty Support - Fall 2026 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll C&I Full-Time Faculty Support - Fall 2026 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title C&I Full-Time Faculty Support - Fall 2026 Description of GA Assignment GA: Faculty Support - Assist faculty, services may include tasks as supervising laboratories under their supervision; grading quizzes, homework, and other projects; and assist with other course and research related duties as assigned. Job Description Summary The Faculty Support GA will work collaboratively with faculty to support teaching, scholarship, and program initiatives within the Department of Curriculum and Instruction. Responsibilities may include serving as a teaching assistant, developing instructional and program resources, supporting student engagement, assisting with event planning, participating in research-related activities, and completing other duties as assigned. Adhere to Marshall University and the College of Education and Professional Development’s professional expectations, FERPA requirements, confidentiality expectations, and communication practices. Department Educational Doctoral Program - MU2840 Location MUGC - Marshall University South Charleston Semester Fall Semester Hours Per Week Full Time (20 hrs a week) Qualifications Required Qualifications Education Earned master’s degree in education or a related field. Admission to and continued enrollment in the Education Specialist (Ed.S.) or Doctor of Education (Ed.D.) major in Curriculum and Instruction. Experience Basic proficiency with computer applications and educational technologies. Preferred Qualifications Education Completed course work or professional interests related to teaching, learning, assessment, or research. Experience Experience teaching in an education setting. Posting Detail Information Posting Number MU3150GA Open Date 08/17/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
