    "https://marshall.peopleadmin.com/postings/32848": {
      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | MAMC Workforce Development Program Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll MAMC Workforce Development Program Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Banner Position Number R10905 Position Title MAMC Workforce Development Program Manager Classification Title MURC-Managers, All Other Department Robert C. Byrd Institute - RC1511 Job Description The Marshall Advanced Manufacturing Center ( MAMC ), formerly called RCBI , is accepting resumes for a Workforce Development Program Manager. Position Description: The MAMC Workforce Development Program Manager is responsible for supporting program clients in obtaining training, industry-recognized certifications, apprenticeship and pre-apprenticeship opportunities, and academic degrees that best align with their career goals. The Workforce Manager is part of MAMC’s Workforce Development Team and reports directly to the Apprenticeship Unit Director. The position will split time between MAMC’s primary facilities in Huntington and South Charleston. As part of the MAMC Workforce Development Team, the Manager will work closely with the Team to plan, coordinate, and implement skills programs, apprenticeships, and pre apprenticeships for individuals and businesses. This position will work directly with people and businesses developing customized, in demand training opportunities. Location OTHR - Other Off-Campus Location Salary Range Salary is commensurate with education, experience and internal equity Required Qualifications Education Bachelor’s degree is required. Experience Success and experience working in a high-performance, collaborative peer group environment; possess strong program management skills and the ability to manage complex, multifaceted projects is required. Must possess excellent verbal and written skills as well as the ability to cultivate new and existing relationships. Candidate is required to be proficient in MS Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Outlook, and use of audiovisual equipment . Candidates must have the ability to travel. Preferred Qualifications Education Experience Independent, results-focused, highly organized self-starter with supervisory skills is preferred. Experience with federal grants and Salesforce, MS Access or another database system is a plus. Demonstrated effectiveness as a leader, 3 years of experience in a team management role is preferred. Sophisticated personal networking and relationship building skills is preferred. Posting Detail Information Posting Number MR0865 Open Date 06/01/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
