    "https://marshall.peopleadmin.com/postings/32735": {
      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Postdoctoral Research Fellow",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Postdoctoral Research Fellow Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Postdoctoral Research Fellow Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Banner Position Number R10917 Position Title Postdoctoral Research Fellow Classification Title MURC-Biological Scientists Department SOM-BioMedical Science - RC5130 Job Description The Li Laboratory in the Department of Biomedical Sciences at the Marshall University Joan C. Edwards School of Medicine is seeking a highly motivated, organized, and detail-oriented Postdoctoral Research Fellow to join an NIH -funded research program investigating the molecular mechanisms by which Na⁺/K⁺-ATPase (sodium pump) signaling and sex hormones regulate thrombosis, vascular inflammation, and cardiovascular disease. The successful candidate will work in a collaborative and multidisciplinary research environment focused on cardiovascular biology, vascular inflammation, and thrombotic disease. This is a full-time, benefits-eligible, at-will position. The successful candidate will complete a three-month probationary period before transitioning to an annual appointment, contingent upon satisfactory performance and continued funding. The ability to work independently while contributing effectively within a collaborative research team. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. · Strong organizational skills with meticulous attention to detail. Experience working with laboratory animals, particularly mice. Demonstrated experience with standard molecular and cellular biology techniques, including PCR , quantitative PCR , Western blotting, immunohistochemistry/immunofluorescence, molecular cloning, co-immunoprecipitation, and related methods. Experience in mammalian cell culture, transient or stable gene transfection, and functional cellular assays. Proficiency with ImageJ/Fiji, GraphPad Prism, Adobe Creative Cloud (e.g., Illustrator and Photoshop), and other scientific data analysis, visualization, and data management software. Location MURC - Marshall University Research Corporation Salary Range Salary is commensurate on education and experience. Required Qualifications Education Ph.D., M.D., or M.D./Ph.D. in Biomedical Sciences, Biology, Biochemistry, Physiology, Pharmacology, Medicine, or a closely related discipline. Experience Experience working with laboratory animals, particularly mice. Demonstrated experience with standard molecular and cellular biology techniques, including PCR , quantitative PCR , Western blotting, immunohistochemistry/immunofluorescence, molecular cloning, co-immunoprecipitation, and related methods. Experience in mammalian cell culture, transient or stable gene transfection, and functional cellular assays. Preferred Qualifications Education Experience Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to applicants with: At least two first-author publications accepted or published in peer-reviewed journals relevant to cardiovascular biology, thrombosis, vascular biology, or related biomedical fields. Experience with intracellular signaling, platelet biology, thrombosis, vascular biology, mouse models of cardiovascular disease, or microsurgical techniques. Experience with flow cytometry, confocal microscopy, transcriptomic analysis, or bioinformatics is desirable but not required. Posting Detail Information Posting Number MR0891 Open Date 08/18/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Ph.D., M.D., or M.D./Ph.D. in Biomedical Sciences, Biology, Biochemistry, Physiology, Pharmacology, Medicine, or a closely related discipline? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents CV or Resume Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://marshall.peopleadmin.com/postings/32235": {
      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Contract Analyst Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Contract Analyst Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Banner Position Number R10900 Position Title Contract Analyst Classification Title MURC-Finance Specialist, Other Department MURC - Financial Administration - RC1516 Job Description Position Summary The Contract Analyst position is a newly created shared position between the Financial Department and the Subaward and Contract Compliance Department. This role reviews service agreement invoices for compliance prior to payment, works with departments to resolve invoice issues, and supports the closeout of contractual agreements. The Contract Analyst works closely with the Senior Finance Officer and the Associate Director of Subaward and Contract Compliance to ensure accurate and compliant processing of contractual invoices and timely closeout of funds. Essential Duties and Responsibilities ·Review service agreements to verify that invoices submitted for payment align with contractual terms, scope of work, and approved funding · Identify invoice discrepancies or compliance issues and work directly with departments to resolve concerns before payments are processed · Processing of invoice payments for weekly check runs. · Serve as a point of contact for departments regarding invoice compliance questions related to service agreements · Support the closeout of contractual agreements by ensuring all required invoices have been submitted, reviewed, and paid · Coordinate with the Grant Invoicing Office when ending fund notifications are issued to departments · Prepare and distribute detailed transaction reports for ending funds and work with departments to reconcile outstanding charges to ensure all invoices are submitted and paid prior to closeout ·Provide guidance to departments on contractual invoicing requirements and best practices · All other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities · Strong analytical abilities and familiarity with the Microsoft Office Suite, especially Excel. · Experience with Cayuse and Banner a plus Location MURC - Marshall University Research Corporation Salary Range $55,000 - Salary is commensurate with education, experience and internal equity Required Qualifications Education Bachelor’s degree Experience 2 years of relevant experience Preferred Qualifications Education Experience Posting Detail Information Posting Number MR0872 Open Date 06/24/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree or higher? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://marshall.peopleadmin.com/postings/32031": {
      "title": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Marshall University Employment Opportunities | Fall 2026 - GA - LCOB Accreditation Help Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus ID Office Title IX IT Service Desk Parking Payroll Fall 2026 - GA - LCOB Accreditation Help Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Fall 2026 - GA - LCOB Accreditation Help Description of GA Assignment GA: Faculty Support - Assist faculty, services may include tasks as supervising laboratories under their supervision; grading quizzes, homework, and other projects; and assist with other course and research related duties as assigned. Job Description Summary Faculty Support, Lewis College of Business • Assist faculty and staff with data related to accreditation. • Provide research support for the LCOB’s faculty • Assist with editing, researching articles, and creating new research. • Assist with LCOB led community activities • Responsible for assisting faculty with day-to-day projects as they come up. Department Dean - Lewis College of Business - MU2300 Location MU - Marshall University Semester Fall Semester Hours Per Week Full Time (20 hrs a week) Qualifications Required Qualifications Education Bachelor’s Degree Experience Knowledge of various versions of windows and general PC hardware. Must be able to perform all essential job duties as outlined in the job description. Preferred Qualifications Education Experience Posting Detail Information Posting Number MU3074GA Open Date 06/02/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Dis