alary is commensurate with education, experience, and internal equity Salary Type Salary Time Type Full-Time Work Location MU - Marshall University Qualifications Must be able to perform all essential job duties as outlined in the job description. Required Qualifications Education Master’s degree or higher in counseling, clinical psychology, counseling psychology, social work, marriage and family therapy, or a closely related mental health field. Licensed or license-eligible as a mental health provider in the State of West Virginia, with the ability to obtain appropriate West Virginia licensure within a specified timeframe following hire. Demonstrated experience providing mental health services to college students, athletes, emerging adults, or individuals in high-performance environments. Demonstrated education, training, or experience in sport psychology, mental performance, performance psychology, or a closely related area. Knowledge of professional ethics, confidentiality, and applicable laws and regulations governing mental health practice. Strong interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills with the ability to work effectively within an interdisciplinary environment. Experience Two years Counseling experience, crisis intervention experience. Must be able to perform all essential job duties as outlined in job description. Preferred Qualifications Education Experience Experience providing mental health or mental performance services within collegiate athletics. Certified Mental Performance Consultant® ( CMPC ) credential or progress toward CMPC certification. Experience developing or facilitating mental wellness, sport psychology, or mental performance programming for individuals or teams. Experience working with NCAA student-athletes or within another high-performance environment. Experience collaborating with coaches, athletic trainers, strength and conditioning professionals, or other members of an interdisciplinary performance team Posting Detail Information Posting Number MU1283E Open Date 08/24/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master’s degree or higher in counseling, clinical psychology, counseling psychology, social work, marriage and family therapy, or a closely related mental health field? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Marshall University One John Marshall Drive Huntington, WV 25755 Copyright © 2020 Marshall University | An Equal Opportunity University | Accreditation | Consumer Information and Disclosures To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
